## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses mastery of modern CSS techniques including CSS Grid, container queries, responsive design principles, and accessibility considerations for real-world product interfaces.

## Key Concepts
- CSS Grid layout with auto-sizing columns
- Container queries for container-based responsiveness
- Equal-height card layouts using grid alignment
- Motion preferences and performance optimization
- Content Layout Shift (CLS) prevention during resize operations

## Code Example
```css
.grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
  gap: 1rem;
  align-items: stretch;
  container-type: inline-size;
}

@container (max-width: 63.99em) {
  .grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
}

@container (max-width: 31em) {
  .grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 2rem;
  }
}

.card {
  transform: translateY(0);
  transition: transform 0.2s ease;
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
  .card {
    animation: fadeInUp 0.4s ease-out;
  }

  .card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
  }
}

@keyframes fadeInUp {
  from {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(20px);
  }
  to {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }
}
```

