## Why This Is Asked

Tests beginner ability to reason about Lighthouse issues, bundle splitting, and lazy-loading with a realistic small app.

## Key Concepts

- Code splitting with dynamic imports
- Lazy-loading assets/images
- Visibility gate using IntersectionObserver
- Lighthouse CI validation

## Code Example

```javascript
// lazy load heavy widget
const Heavy = React.lazy(() => import('./HeavyWidget'));

function Gate() {
  const ref = useRef(null);
  const [show, setShow] = useState(false);
  useEffect(() => {
    const io = new IntersectionObserver(([e]) => { if (e.isIntersecting) setShow(true); }, {threshold: 0.1});
    if (ref.current) io.observe(ref.current);
    return () => io.disconnect();
  }, []);
  return (
    <div ref={ref}>
      {show ? (
        <Suspense fallback={<div>Loading…</div>}><Heavy/></Suspense>
      ) : null}
    </div>
  );
}
```

